version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - prompt injection
  - LLM evaluation
  - oversight
  - pre-registration
abstract: >
  The grading code, ledger audits and pre-registered experiment designs of a research
  programme that tests where one language model checking another one's work breaks down.
  Tasks carry exact integer answers (arithmetic, table lookup, code tracing, fixed facts),
  so outputs are graded against the answer rather than by a judge model; runs used local
  open-weight models on one GPU. Contains 28 Python modules; 75 designs
  (the 73 pre-registered ones, one corrected re-run and one template) with the
  latest graded result of each that has one (70 rows, 214 cells; per-item
  values kept, raw model text removed); the retraction ledger (28 records);
  and the re-serve supersessions. reproduce.py
  recomputes 178 stored verdicts from their per-item values, runs a planted-defect
  canary against nine ledger audits, and runs the instrument controls, offline with numpy
  as the only dependency.
